## SQ-PF-02 | /cdevperf dump and the perf report
@group A
@commands After 2 min, `/cdevperf dump smoke`; copy the file here, `python3 tools/perf/perf_report.py <file>` (PF-15)
@pass Chat says saved; the report's "Measured by the pack's hooks" has ticks, a row per dimension, handlers as `server_scripts:<file>:<line>`, entity and block entity types
@fails Depends on: SQ-PF-01
@reviewed 2026-11-21
@from batches/r1102b/s3_A.qb
# judge-7, r1120nv, 2026-11-21: a pig and a hopper tick during the recording (the idle flat world has none); the report is
# HTML now (perf/reports/, path on the `report:` line), so the shell prints its text
> forceload add 0 0
> summon minecraft:pig 0 -60 0 {Tags:["pf02"]}
> setblock 1 -60 0 minecraft:hopper
sleep 5
> cdevperf status
expect recording '
> cdevperf dump smoke
waitlog \[cdevperf\] recording saved to 300
capture PFF recording saved to (\S+)
shell python3 -I $INST/tools/perf/perf_report.py {PFF} > ../pf02_report.txt 2>&1; echo "exit $?"; cat ../pf02_report.txt; r=$(grep -o "report: .*" ../pf02_report.txt | cut -d" " -f2); python3 -I -c "import re,sys,html; t=open(sys.argv[1]).read(); t=re.sub(r'<script.*?</script>|<style.*?</style>','',t,flags=re.S); t=re.sub(r'\s+',' ',html.unescape(re.sub(r'<[^>]+>',' ',t))); i=t.find('Measured by the pack'); print(t[i:i+5000])" "$r"
> kill @e[tag=pf02]
> setblock 1 -60 0 minecraft:air
look rows/SQ-PF-02.shell.txt: ticks, a row per dimension, handlers as <script pack>:<file>:<line> (jar scripts since the carve), entity and block entity types (the pig, the hopper)

